        "guide_13": {
          "type": "guide",
          "settings": {
            "category": "Women",
            "title": "How to Measure Women's Pants and Shorts",
            "steps": "Waist: For a high rise waist, measure all the way around the point you would like to wear the pants.This is usually at or covering your navel Allow a bit of extra room for movement and for tucking a shirt. For a Mid-Rise, measure all the way around your waist mid way between the hips and the navel.For a low rise waist, measure around your hips, on the lower part of your hips and decidedly lower than your Mid- waist.\nSeat/Hip: Standing with your feet together, measure around the fullest part of your hip (approx. 7-8\" below the waist). Don’t forget to keep the tape level.\nInseam: Best taken from an existing pair of pants you like. Measure along the garment inseam from your crotch seam to the hem.",
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/wmnpent.png",
            "image_2": "shopify://shop_images/womenpentsecond.png"
          }
        },
